### Sample requests for IntelliJ's HTTP Client (run with `docker compose up`).

### A valid submission: 202 with the new id
POST http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "birthday": "1990-12-10",
  "reminderWindowDays": 7,
  "giftIdeas": "A first edition of her notes"
}

> {% client.global.set("birthdayId", response.body.id); %}

### Several bad fields: 400 listing each one
POST http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "  ",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "birthday": "2023-02-30",
  "reminderWindowDays": 15
}

### An unknown field: 400
POST http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "5b0e5a3c-1f6e-4a52-9a3b-2f1d6c7e8a90",
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "birthday": "1990-12-10",
  "reminderWindowDays": 7
}

### Malformed JSON: 400
POST http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Ada

### The list, soonest birthday first: 200
GET http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays

### The entry from the first request: 200, or 404 for a moment while it's in flight
GET http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays/{{birthdayId}}

### A malformed id: 400
GET http://localhost:3000/api/birthdays/not-a-uuid

### An unknown route: 404
GET http://localhost:3000/api/unknown
